# rm255, the chorus in the stair (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm255
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for rmx_sigrun_wickham
written_by codex
title the chorus in the stair
fits stage=adult|old
prefers humour=merry talk=chatty
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=merry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk leaves_a_gap_in_a_sea_chorus_for_the_stair_to_answer
likes mutton_stew riddles fresh_straw first_warm_day
dislikes night_noise bad_manners
fears the_rattle_after_dusk the_loss_of_a_tune
hopes a_street_where_every_door_has_a_verse
topics pastimes +0.6 home +0.4 food +0.3 memories +0.3 travel -0.2
styles comfort=company gossip=reticent refuse=playful tease=gentle
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# hums the hauling part of a sea song and leaves a beat for a loose hinge to answer, turns riddles over at leisure, and chooses company in small doses.

words
oath! = Barnacles in the bass | Split the chorus
saying! = Leave a beat for the boards | A good refrain can climb alone
bassstep = the deep note | that low carrying hum
creaknote = the squeal in the hinge | a long wooden creak
quickstep = two little taps | the short double knock
strawtip = a pale straw tip | a little bent straw
blank = one empty beat | the place I leave open
spoonrest = a notch worn by a spoon | my little spoon notch
potcorner = the brown bit at the edge | a good brown corner of stew
seatboard = a wide flat board | a comfortable bit of timber
gustline = a whistle under a door | a thin note of wind
lidrum = a tin lid | the lid of a small tin pot
hush = a soft rest | a pause wide as a breath

any
opinion @1 dole for 2 : A free bowl might be the reason there's a voice left to join the chorus.
opinion @1 houses against 2 : Wooden boards answer me better than the houses of the mighty ever have.
opinion @1 sump for 1 : Nobody sings alone in a building with boards as thin as ours.
opinion @1 road against 1 : A stirring walking tune won't make a long dark road any safer.
opinion @1 watch against 2 : A good steady tread is a comfort, until it stops outside the wrong door.
opinion @1 newcomers against 1 : Give me a minute to get used to another measure on the stair.
opinion @1 merchants against 1 : Prices climb another octave between one dip in my purse and the next.

grown
line @1 greet : I was humming. Words will do just as well.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : A new voice is welcome to a few quiet measures.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning's trying out a thin high note.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. Even the far windows have settled to a hum.
line @1 greet.return : That's the answer my tune was waiting for.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Oh good. A familiar pair of ears.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : I heard you through the clattering.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : The greeting carries. You needn't strain.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Kin can join in halfway through a bar.
line @1 again.open : Back in time for the second verse, I see.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : My dear familiar footfall! Over this way.
line @1 farewell : Take a decent tune home with you.
line @1 farewell.return : And don't let a squeaking gate give you the last word.
line @1 react.news : Tell it once at your own pace.
line @1 react.news.new : There wasn't a note of that in my hearing.
line @1 react.news.known : Yes, that's been sung round here once already.
line @1 react.news.doubt : That chorus seems a trifle out of time.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I'd leave a good long silence for that.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : I could hum the glad part twice for news like that.
line @1 ask.how : What tune would fit your morning?
line @1 answer.how : I'm somewhere between a jig and a sit down.
line @1 thank : You found the note I couldn't reach.
line @1 deflect_thanks : An answering voice does its own share.
line @1 sympathise : You can leave the words out. I'll sit with the quiet.
line @1 reassure : Draw a breath and borrow half of mine.
line @1 decline : I'd better save my wind for the trip home.
line @1 accept_decline : Leave the verse empty. Nobody has to fill it.
line @1 preclose : I'll take what voice I've got left home with me.
line @1 accept_preclose : A talk can have a little rest between verses.
scene hinge_answer
when topic=home|pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A bad hinge makes a fine chorus. | I once tried humming both parts.
b : Does it know when to come in? | A duet all by yourself?
a : Better than I do. Open the door on the fourth beat. | An argument, mostly. The stair's a better partner.

scene next_room
when topic=home self.quarter=sump
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In our bit of the Sump you can hear a pot thinking about boiling. | Some walls let every tune through except the pretty ones.
b : Thinking, you say? | Can't you move the chair?
a : The lid starts whispering long before it has to shout. | Tried that. The wall had a much larger chair.

scene thin_company
when topic=friends
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I find one visitor cheering and six visitors six visits too long. | I'd have company in spoonfuls.
b : Where does the second one go? | Sugar or medicine?
a : Into the account for next week. | Stew, of course. I'd never refuse a spoon of that.

scene straw_scratch
when topic=home self.likes=fresh_straw
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Listen to fresh straw when you lay your cheek down. | #strawtip.capitalize# makes a very light baton.
b : Is there a tune in bedding too? | What would you conduct?
a : No, a small argument. Everybody wants to lie the other way up. | A few contented snores, if the night goes well.

scene warm_day
when topic=season here.season=spring
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The first warmth makes the stair rail pleasant to touch. | A mild breeze makes the door sing half a note lower.
b : That's your sign of spring? | Is that enough to notice?
a : My hand meets the rail a deal more often than it meets a flower. | To me. Been carrying the winter part in my throat for ages.

scene stew_supper
when topic=food self.likes=mutton_stew
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Leave me #potcorner# if you're serving mutton. | I'd trade three thin meals for one stew that held a spoon upright.
b : That's the bit that catches. | How would you eat it?
a : That's the bit with something to say for itself. | Sideways, laughing.

scene loose_riddle
when topic=pastimes self.likes=riddles
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : What can go downstairs without leaving its seat? | I prefer the answer that turns up too late.
b : Your humming, I suppose. | Too late for what?
a : A squeak from my chair as well. That's a riddle with room to spare. | For winning. Then you get to enjoy it for nothing.

scene hush_hours
when topic=smalltalk here.time=night
does tell.complaint / sympathise / assess
a : A pot left rolling on a floor at night takes all night to fall flat. | Look at all this quiet I've been saving. One slam and it's spent.
b : Sounds dreadful to lie through. | I'll go gently.
a : Especially when my head's already begun supplying the words. | If it does slam we'll call it a single drumbeat and be done.

scene courtesy
when topic=smalltalk self.dislikes=bad_manners
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A wolf who knocks and doesn't wait has wasted a perfectly good knock. | I've no use for elbows that introduce themselves first.
b : What ought the caller to wait for? | Even at market?
a : An answer or a respectable lack of one. | A crowded place is when a mouth ought to get there ahead.

scene dust_lungs
when topic=health self.age>=60
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : My knees have picked up a harmony I never taught them. | I'm old enough to stop halfway and enjoy how far I've been.
b : Does it hurt to hear it? | A fine privilege.
a : There's pain and there's noise. I take a little pleasure telling those apart. | Yes. Took a quite unreasonable time to acquire it.

scene away_shore
when topic=travel here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A song about the sea can give the whole Sound a travelling stage. | I like the wharf better in a tune than in a shoving crowd.
b : How do you put a bay on a stage? | Even the smell of tar?
a : One long hum, with the gulls doing short business over it. | My version comes with the smell turned down.

scene neighbour_seat
when topic=home self.neighbour
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd save #self.neighbour# the chair farthest from the squeak. | It would please me to share a quiet spoon of stew with #self.neighbour#.
b : Where does that leave you? | You could bring a song for afterwards.
a : Where I can work the squeak into our conversation. | I'd bring a lid to keep the song under, just in case.

scene plain_supper
when topic=prices|times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Lean stew has very good acoustics. | A short purse can put a long pause between meals.
b : Much room in the pot? | You do sound tired.
a : Plenty of echoes and not much mutton. | The pause is longer than my joke about it, certainly.

scene cart_rhythm
when topic=travel|times world.wagons=late
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A missing cart wheel puts the town song out of time. | With the wagons behind time you'd expect a quieter street.
b : You hear a missing wheel? | Isn't it?
a : Hear where the noise ought to be. That's late wagons for you. | Too many voices wondering what's keeping the wagons.

scene soft_gossip
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.gossip / react.self / assess
a : I heard something I'd rather hum than speak. | Plenty of names would fit in the chorus I leave out.
b : Can I guess from the tune? | Would mine fit?
a : I'll change key if you try. | Yours and mine can have the pleasure of staying out together.

scene news_word
when topic=news world.news
does tell.news / react.self / assess
a : The words I caught from #world.news_from# go like this: #world.news#. | #world.news.capitalize#. Put #world.news_from# beside that in your recollection.
b : Is the tune important? | That's all you can place?
a : No tune at all. News travels oddly enough in plain words. | That's all I'll give a firm note to.

scene bolted_tune
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : On my first proper try at a sea tune I swallowed half the words. | I can't remember the first verse I learned.
b : Did you catch your breath? | Does it bother you?
a : Yes, and acquired a taste for half the words. | No. There's a lovely wide space at the beginning.

scene winter_rain
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Every gutter keeps a different time. | Rain on thin tin can spoil a singer's concentration.
b : Which do you follow? | Too loud?
a : The slow reluctant one. I can breathe between its drops. | Too good. I keep stopping to admire it.

story lost_note [topic=memories|pastimes]
  : I once pitched a tune so low the chair began to shake.
  : Stopped singing and the chair went on trembling.
  b : Had the tune got loose?
  : A wagon was going by. I took a bow anyway since nobody was looking.

story stew_bell [topic=memories|food]
  : Tried to lift a stew lid with a spoon and sent the lid rolling round the room.
  : It went three times round a stool before it dropped.
  b : Was the stew all right?
  : Cold by the time I finished making up a decent verse to the lid.

story straw_letter [topic=home|memories]
  : A pair of long straws once crossed each other like the first letter of my name.
  : I felt obliged to write the rest with pieces to match.
  b : Could anybody read it?
  : Possibly the cat. It settled on my signature with entire satisfaction.

rule @gap_rail
when concept=bark here.place=street
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Two taps and a pause. Anybody care to do the high bit?

rule @pot_hum
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say I can hear my appetite rehearsing the supper verse.

rule @nod_off
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A quiet lid would make a lovely lullaby.

rule @warm_room
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Rain with a bass part. That's an ambitious little gutter.

dlg @1 resident.hub : There's half a verse free for you in this conversation.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#. Your name comes into the tune very nicely.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : Quietly now. We might get to enjoy ourselves without an audience.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : I won't try harmony today. Say your bit from there.
dlg @1 resident.job : Watching takes less wind than singing. I make time to do both.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : #world.news.capitalize#. Heard that account from #world.news_from# without any chorus attached.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : Some wolf or other ought to drop the tune. I can be that wolf.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Don't take the squeak personally on your way out.
graft resident.hub
choice When does the stair come into the song? -> fourth_tread
node fourth_tread
say After the long low note. The third board used to chime in too, but it wore out or grew shy. Can't say I blame it.
choice Do the boards know many tunes? -> timber_tunes
choice I'll listen on my way out. -> hub
node timber_tunes
say Just one answer between the lot of them. Quite enough to carry a conversation if everybody says it at the right moment.
choice A good moment to change the subject. -> hub
choice I'll leave a silence behind me. -> bye
